1) Run SELECT database, table, is_readonly, absolute_delay, zookeeper_exception FROM system.replicas to locate the failed tables;
2) A large absolute_delay means the replica cannot keep up — check the replica node's IO and its merge queue (system.replication_queue);
3) ALL_REPLICAS_LOST usually means the metadata in ZooKeeper is gone, so verify the data on a healthy replica and then run SYSTEM RESTORE REPLICA;
4) Route queries to healthy shards while recovering so they stop failing.

